  "definition": "A handwritten demo is an informal, analogue artefact\u2014such as a hand-annotated sketch, cost sheet, or prototype diagram\u2014used to communicate design intent, feasibility, or scope before digital tooling is applied. In the context of knowledge graph construction and AI-assisted workflows, handwritten demos often serve as raw input for multimodal AI systems capable of recognising, digitising, and annotating unstructured human-authored content.",
